#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119650 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119836 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "abef3da6-252e-51e4-b816-9ef7233b9a5d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line in Vector Form and a Plane in Dot Product Form"}] :question/id #uuid "1d809050-9477-5de6-8c95-7294804e7b69" :question/math-academy-id "e-4943" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $\\Pi$ with equations\n\n$$\nl: \\mathbf{r} = \\langle 5,3,-4 \\rangle + t \\langle 4,-2,-3 \\rangle, \\qquad \t\\Pi: \\mathbf{r} \\cdot \\langle -7,5,1 \\rangle = -65.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's write the equation of the line as \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r} = \\langle 5+4t , 3-2t, -4-3t \\rangle.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $\\mathbf{r} = \\langle 5+4t , 3-2t, -4-3t \\rangle$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨-7,5,1⟩ & =-65 \\\\ ⟨5+4t,3-2t,-4-3t⟩\\cdot ⟨-7,5,1⟩ & =-65 \\\\ -7(5+4t)+5(3-2t)+(-4-3t) & =-65 \\\\ -35-28t+15-10t-4-3t & =-65 \\\\ -41t & =-41 \\\\ t & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the position vector $\\mathbf{p}$ of the intersection point is obtained by substituting $t=1$ into the equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨5+4(1),3-2(1),-4-3(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨9,1,-7⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(9 , 1, -7).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119651 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119837 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "caf29808-4551-56a0-ac86-a4587a06fc0f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line and a Plane Given in Other Forms"}] :question/id #uuid "c1576b30-9142-5884-b654-7ade7a765ec7" :question/math-academy-id "e-4944" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $\\Pi$ with equations\n\n$$\nl: \\mathbf{r} = \\langle 1,3,1 \\rangle + t \\langle 2,1,0 \\rangle, \\qquad  \\Pi:4x-3y+2z-7 = 0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the equation of the line as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r} = \\langle 1+2t , 3+t, 1 \\rangle .\n$$\n\nLet's also write the equation of the plane in the dot product form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x-3y+2z-7 & =0 \\\\ 4x-3y+2z & =7 \\\\ ⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨4,-3,2⟩ & =7 \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨4,-3,2⟩ & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $\\mathbf{r} = \\langle 1+2t , 3+t, 1 \\rangle$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨4,-3,2⟩ & =7 \\\\ ⟨1+2t,3+t,1⟩\\cdot ⟨4,-3,2⟩ & =7 \\\\ 4(1+2t)-3(3+t)+2\\cdot 1 & =7 \\\\ 4+8t-9-3t+2 & =7 \\\\ 5t & =10 \\\\ t & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $\\mathbf{p}$ of the intersection point $P,$ we substitute $t=2$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨1+2(2),3+(2),1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5,5,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(5 , 5, 1).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119652 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119838 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "82e761b5-ec1c-549d-b726-e0909cfe460b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line in Parametric Form and a Plane in Cartesian Form"}] :question/id #uuid "f952e670-a673-5c15-913b-c396e8885142" :question/math-academy-id "e-4945" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $\\Pi$ with equations\n![](images/64/64a3661b0699fbde542ed1709bacf569f681477a5f824f0650b07d9060b82dae.svg)" :question/worked-solution "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x+4y+6z+25 & =0 \\\\ 3(3-4t)+4(-1+2t)+6(2+3t)+25 & =0 \\\\ 9-12t-4+8t+12+18t+25 & =0 \\\\ 14t & =-42 \\\\ t & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $\\mathbf{p}$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=-3$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=3-4(-3)=15 \\\\ y=-1+2(-3)=-7 \\\\ z=2+3(-3)=-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is $P(15,-7,-7).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186442983 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119836 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "abef3da6-252e-51e4-b816-9ef7233b9a5d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line in Vector Form and a Plane in Dot Product Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8834e13a-22fa-5aac-a999-328918db52aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5,2,5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442967} {:answer/id #uuid "96d49a2f-474b-5bba-b6c4-17e8726cbd43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442968} {:answer/id #uuid "b83d1b54-86e9-5e63-af2b-8d6d7fdb32d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,2,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442970} {:answer/id #uuid "f64b86a2-04c6-5e9a-9cf2-346fe66c641a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-7,2,-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442976} {:answer/id #uuid "fa261700-7670-52be-9dc1-2ffc7832aa15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-4,2,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442978}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8834e13a-22fa-5aac-a999-328918db52aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5,2,5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442967} :answer-field/id #uuid "c7e90ddb-8e9f-5cb4-bec1-a99d63f38772" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442981}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8e5d0c94-6cbf-5053-b8da-ce1333f1257b" :question/math-academy-id "q-108308" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨-1,2,1⟩+t⟨3,0,2⟩,\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨1,-1,2⟩=13.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's write the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨-1+3t,2,1+2t⟩.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨-1+3t,2,1+2t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨1,-1,2⟩ & =13 \\\\ ⟨-1+3t,2,1+2t⟩\\cdot ⟨1,-1,2⟩ & =13 \\\\ 1(-1+3t)-2+2(1+2t) & =13 \\\\ -1+3t-2+2+4t & =13 \\\\ 7t & =14 \\\\ t & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$ is obtained by substituting $t=2$ into the equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨-1+3(2),2,1+2(2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5,2,5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(5,2,5).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186442984 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119836 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "abef3da6-252e-51e4-b816-9ef7233b9a5d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line in Vector Form and a Plane in Dot Product Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00128b0b-75f1-5ff4-8a3e-54c15cf052dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-3,-1,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442960} {:answer/id #uuid "0db1cb8d-ae91-58aa-ba6d-996ec7b29ea2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-7,1,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442961} {:answer/id #uuid "25dfd479-4874-55fc-ac79-5aafbe7a30f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442962} {:answer/id #uuid "66855eaf-d25e-59dd-8568-e9296afde634" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,-3,4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442965} {:answer/id #uuid "bc96ece3-ea6d-5cb5-94a3-9ae65aed87a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5,-5,5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442971}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "25dfd479-4874-55fc-ac79-5aafbe7a30f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442962} :answer-field/id #uuid "3a04dab5-4de0-5a23-bb85-4c890b9f023c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442979}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a985335b-cba4-5e25-b462-ecfeb2395155" :question/math-academy-id "q-108315" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨1,-3,4⟩+t⟨4,-2,1⟩,\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨-2,-3,2⟩=1.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's write the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨1+4t,-3-2t,4+t⟩.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨1+4t,-3-2t,4+t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨-2,-3,2⟩ & =1 \\\\ ⟨1+4t,-3-2t,4+t⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,-3,2⟩ & =1 \\\\ -2(1+4t)+(-3)(-3-2t)+2\\cdot (4+t) & =1 \\\\ -2-8t+9+6t+8+2t & =1 \\\\ 15 & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation has no solution. Therefore, we conclude that the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ do not intersect."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186475947 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119836 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "abef3da6-252e-51e4-b816-9ef7233b9a5d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line in Vector Form and a Plane in Dot Product Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10f49541-bf17-51d7-9f75-37616f1a6089" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,-1,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475468} {:answer/id #uuid "60c57a2e-889c-5474-81d3-a55d65fdd34b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(8,2,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475585} {:answer/id #uuid "813ea0c8-6a02-5346-b587-75a643aadca7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,4,-4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475635} {:answer/id #uuid "b4214275-5327-55f6-a028-7523f95b454a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5,3,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475710} {:answer/id #uuid "bbf64d63-9b14-5d35-91c0-7a22161af6ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475730}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bbf64d63-9b14-5d35-91c0-7a22161af6ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475730} :answer-field/id #uuid "1cedb4ab-8127-56c0-a22d-80bf5a1ac4a8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475837}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8ef5750d-a5da-50af-8419-8b1661dfe47b" :question/math-academy-id "q-108319" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨5,3,-2⟩+t⟨3,-1,2⟩,\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨-2,4,5⟩=8.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's write the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨5+3t,3-t,-2+2t⟩.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨5+3t,3-t,-2+2t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨-2,4,5⟩ & =8 \\\\ ⟨5-3t,3-t,-2+2t⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,4,5⟩ & =8 \\\\ -2(5+3t)+4(3-t)+5\\cdot (-2+2t) & =8 \\\\ -10-6t+12-4t-10+10t & =8 \\\\ -8 & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation has no solution. Therefore, we conclude that the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ do not intersect."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244121 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119838 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "82e761b5-ec1c-549d-b726-e0909cfe460b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line in Parametric Form and a Plane in Cartesian Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "600b8aef-da6c-5a05-9753-24914a3499d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(9,4,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242041} {:answer/id #uuid "7687f722-fb74-5a86-8afb-5ba790d4f143" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(11,5,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242232} {:answer/id #uuid "a77e3a01-860e-5d47-a380-4a2919fe0ab4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,0,4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242649} {:answer/id #uuid "b30eea27-088d-5354-8ef8-bcf626ddf460" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1,-1,5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242738} {:answer/id #uuid "f57050d6-b5e9-5c5f-838d-d66ca290b074" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243349}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b30eea27-088d-5354-8ef8-bcf626ddf460" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1,-1,5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242738} :answer-field/id #uuid "6652b296-a21e-518a-9c5b-d45f374f2267" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243639}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7d4770f9-017d-5451-ade2-ef9bc61cba33" :question/math-academy-id "q-108323" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:\\{\\begin{aligned}x=7+2t \\\\ y=3+t \\\\ z=1-t\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:x-3y+2z=12.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-3y+2z & =12 \\\\ 1(7+2t)-3(3+t)+2(1-t) & =12 \\\\ 7+2t-9-3t+2-2t & =12 \\\\ -3t & =12 \\\\ t & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=-4$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=7+2(-4)=-1 \\\\ y=3+(-4)=-1 \\\\ z=1-(-4)=5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is $P(-1,-1,5).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186399622 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119838 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "82e761b5-ec1c-549d-b726-e0909cfe460b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line in Parametric Form and a Plane in Cartesian Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c1bd5231-6855-55f3-a5ec-61c58423a2bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,1,9)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399624} {:answer/id #uuid "3a87675b-c089-5d14-9db0-504805f8a6af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,3,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399625} {:answer/id #uuid "02bc6063-6eef-56d8-b50b-eec9ca9b7e38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(4,4,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399626} {:answer/id #uuid "b949434a-7780-5a3d-b4d8-3bbde783f79d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399627} {:answer/id #uuid "44390ca7-20ca-5d21-b624-15837dd00ca6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(8,6,-6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399628}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c1bd5231-6855-55f3-a5ec-61c58423a2bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,1,9)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399624} :answer-field/id #uuid "b8515a18-0ebe-5740-9abf-0e5d9167649f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399623}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "60f0cd70-b4b4-5b35-85ba-563cceee9aad" :question/math-academy-id "q-108326" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:\\{\\begin{aligned}x=6+2t \\\\ y=5+t \\\\ z=-3-3t\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:5x+3y-4z=-43.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x+3y-4z & =-43 \\\\ 5(6+2t)+3(5+t)-4(-3-3t) & =-43 \\\\ 30+10t+15+3t+12+12t & =-43 \\\\ 25t & =-100 \\\\ t & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=-4$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=6+2(-4) \\\\ y=5+(-4) \\\\ z=-3-3(-4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is $P(-2,1,9).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186475922 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119838 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "82e761b5-ec1c-549d-b726-e0909cfe460b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line in Parametric Form and a Plane in Cartesian Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b435381-c5b8-5b4f-8b01-26d7f6d1dc11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5,8,-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475526} {:answer/id #uuid "9dd67c95-9e81-5450-afa6-4d059c19997b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,-13,11)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475676} {:answer/id #uuid "a07f003a-5a14-5c7f-89bb-286c19f2ac04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1,-10,9)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475679} {:answer/id #uuid "b66e1051-daa1-5d8a-8225-891009842666" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(7,14,-7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475718} {:answer/id #uuid "e50752da-554b-56dd-9852-e80a3543b73f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475794}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b66e1051-daa1-5d8a-8225-891009842666" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(7,14,-7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475718} :answer-field/id #uuid "3f1f7c3c-b1c0-5d3b-9ccb-c5f535269a9b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475850}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "231a9d15-2430-5e82-a7fa-b3cd0ec4e91a" :question/math-academy-id "q-108336" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:\\{\\begin{aligned}x=2+t \\\\ y=-1+3t \\\\ z=3-2t\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:2x+y-5z=63.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+y-5z & =63 \\\\ 2(2+t)+(-1+3t)-5(3-2t) & =63 \\\\ 4+2t-1+3t-15+10t & =63 \\\\ 15t & =75 \\\\ t & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=5$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=2+5=7 \\\\ y=-1+3(5)=14 \\\\ z=3-2(5)=-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is $P(7,14,-7).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186475933 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119837 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "caf29808-4551-56a0-ac86-a4587a06fc0f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line and a Plane Given in Other Forms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00592e29-c51c-505e-aa00-3ff92195a878" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-7,12,-13)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475443} {:answer/id #uuid "11e5504e-d64d-5f8c-ac38-3eff267389dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(25,-12,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475471} {:answer/id #uuid "d9c8c1d7-fdbb-512c-ae27-1e5f390a0545" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(13,-6,-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475772} {:answer/id #uuid "de8b2779-f353-540b-b6dc-5741e2b54f02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475782} {:answer/id #uuid "ec08f7ca-621a-5fb1-a281-a7c103129688" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5,3,-7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475805}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "de8b2779-f353-540b-b6dc-5741e2b54f02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475782} :answer-field/id #uuid "4edf1a48-e584-5a56-97e2-8850121c1df9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475855}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "42cfce4b-bf3d-5d7e-8fad-15e0c813875c" :question/math-academy-id "q-108370" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨5,3,-7⟩+t⟨4,-3,2⟩,\\,Π:5x+2y-7z-15=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨5+4t,3-3t,-7+2t⟩.\n$$\n\nLet's also write the equation of the plane in the dot product form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x+2y-7z-15 & =0 \\\\ 5x+2y-7z & =15 \\\\ ⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨5,2,-7⟩ & =15 \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨5,2,-7⟩ & =15\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨5+4t,3-3t,-7+2t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨5,2,-7⟩ & =15 \\\\ ⟨5+4t,3-3t,-7+2t⟩\\cdot ⟨5,2,-7⟩ & =15 \\\\ 5(5+4t)+2(3-3t)-7(-7+2t) & =15 \\\\ 25+20t+6-6t+49-14t & =15 \\\\ 80 & =15.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation has no solution. Therefore, we conclude that the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ do not intersect."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186475912 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119837 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "caf29808-4551-56a0-ac86-a4587a06fc0f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line and a Plane Given in Other Forms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "007d69dc-a2ca-580f-b0f7-74cbcfa1ebdd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475444} {:answer/id #uuid "3a25e529-3954-5987-92eb-d533381cc44b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(25,31,-6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475523} {:answer/id #uuid "52af092c-e727-5f18-8ff7-345347fe6d51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-8,-13,5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475562} {:answer/id #uuid "572842f6-cb5d-5a22-b2c9-50266f22eb6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(13,15,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475570} {:answer/id #uuid "fca47535-789f-5b0b-98b2-271a04ca1b25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-14,-21,7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475823}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3a25e529-3954-5987-92eb-d533381cc44b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(25,31,-6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475523} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8937436-576e-5320-a137-6b981c96167e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475895}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "07e33caa-9650-5834-8d9a-46cc82f723d1" :question/math-academy-id "q-108434" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨1,-1,2⟩+w⟨3,4,-1⟩,\\,Π:r=⟨5,3,-4⟩+s⟨1,0,2⟩+t⟨0,-2,3⟩.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "From the equation of a plane in the parametric form $r=p+tv+sw$, we have that its normal vector is $n=v\\times w.$ In our case, the normal vectors to $Π$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =⟨1,0,2⟩\\times ⟨0,-2,3⟩ \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =4i-3j-2k \\\\  & =⟨4,-3,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane $Π$ in dot product form is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨4,-3,-2⟩ & =⟨5,3,-4⟩\\cdot ⟨4,-3,-2⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨4,-3,-2⟩ & =19.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨1,-1,2⟩+w⟨3,4,-1⟩$ into the equation of the plane in dot product form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨4,-3,-2⟩ & =19 \\\\ ⟨1+3w,-1+4w,2-w⟩\\cdot ⟨4,-3,-2⟩ & =19 \\\\ 4(1+3w)-3(-1+4w)-2(2-w) & =19 \\\\ 4+12w+3-12w-4+2w & =19 \\\\ 2w & =16 \\\\ w & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $q$ of the intersection point $Q,$ we substitute $w=8$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}q & =⟨1+3(8),-1+4(8),2-8⟩ \\\\  & =⟨25,31,-6⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is $Q(25,31,-6).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244184 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119837 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "caf29808-4551-56a0-ac86-a4587a06fc0f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line and a Plane Given in Other Forms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "534563ab-ad8a-52e8-ab28-8e3cb647e59b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,0,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241926} {:answer/id #uuid "7a481cbd-1cba-520f-9744-7029c9f2825f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,4,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242254} {:answer/id #uuid "8328eaca-6d43-51d5-944b-f122a23c3edb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5,4,-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242325} {:answer/id #uuid "9c702dd4-0c20-5809-9cb3-7a9d9423cb1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242545} {:answer/id #uuid "d5b52c46-df5f-5397-a641-365480e0da3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(4,8,-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243071}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7a481cbd-1cba-520f-9744-7029c9f2825f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,4,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242254} :answer-field/id #uuid "62df7e56-3c54-5d7e-9fb7-92c76ce4e2dd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243629}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7ed76edb-2aee-5101-83be-e4a973b64993" :question/math-academy-id "q-108891" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:\\frac{x+2}{3}=\\frac{y}{4}=\\frac{1-z}{2},\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨4,-3,1⟩=-9.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "From the equation of the line $l$, we know that it passes through the point $A(-2,0,1)$ and it is parallel to the vector $v=⟨3,4,-2⟩.$ Therefore, its vector equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =⟨-2,0,1⟩+t⟨3,4,-2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2+3t,4t,1-2t⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨-2+3t,4t,1-2t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨4,-3,1⟩ & =-9 \\\\ ⟨-2+3t,4t,1-2t⟩\\cdot ⟨4,-3,1⟩ & =-9 \\\\ 4(-2+3t)-3(4t)+(1-2t) & =-9 \\\\ -8+12t-12t+1-2t & =-9 \\\\ -2t & =-2 \\\\ t & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P,$ we substitute $t=1$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨-2+3(1),4(1),1-2(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,4,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get $P(1,4,-1).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186475975 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119837 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "caf29808-4551-56a0-ac86-a4587a06fc0f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line and a Plane Given in Other Forms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "35e34ef5-0c0f-566b-94a8-9376d485a3d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0,0,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475516} {:answer/id #uuid "384678c4-4350-5113-9f0f-32d8e2cf6110" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1,1,4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475518} {:answer/id #uuid "92098877-886b-53fa-a483-755c30d71d2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(10,3,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475660} {:answer/id #uuid "b2c22028-564a-5c89-ab16-c9763fcf688a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-7,-3,10)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475706} {:answer/id #uuid "c36ccfc7-634d-5201-b479-3d9288da2e97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475739}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b2c22028-564a-5c89-ab16-c9763fcf688a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-7,-3,10)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475706} :answer-field/id #uuid "d9d0e6f8-2892-55f4-a237-affcef970729" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475897}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e4fbd5e6-b819-591a-880c-a933bdaba9d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-33082" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨2,3,1⟩+w⟨-3,-2,3⟩,\\,Π:r=⟨-15,1,1⟩+s⟨2,0,2⟩+t⟨1,4,0⟩.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "From the equation of a plane in the parametric form $r=p+tv+sw$, we have that its normal vector is $n=v\\times w.$ In our case, the normal vectors to $Π$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =⟨2,0,2⟩\\times ⟨1,4,0⟩ \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =-8i+2j+8k \\\\  & =⟨-8,2,8⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane $Π$ in dot product form is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-8,2,8⟩ & =⟨-15,1,1⟩\\cdot ⟨-8,2,8⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-8,2,8⟩ & =130.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨2,3,1⟩+w⟨-3,-2,3⟩$ into the equation of the plane in dot product form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨-8,2,8⟩ & =130 \\\\ ⟨2-3w,3-2w,1+3w⟩\\cdot ⟨-8,2,8⟩ & =130 \\\\ -8(2-3w)+2(3-2w)+8(1+3w) & =130 \\\\ -16+24w+6-4w+8+24w & =130 \\\\ 44w & =132 \\\\ w & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $q$ of the intersection point $Q,$ we substitute $w=3$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}q & =⟨2-3(3),3-2(3),1+3(3)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-7,-3,10⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is $Q(-7,-3,10).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314820 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119837 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "caf29808-4551-56a0-ac86-a4587a06fc0f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line and a Plane Given in Other Forms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ff6a580-92b7-5851-bcce-fe10c30be1cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-5,-2,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312490} {:answer/id #uuid "947ae6d9-2a5b-5525-86d2-6a8dcbc0bb2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313166} {:answer/id #uuid "ae867fd0-223f-5656-84a8-6dd4a2746db7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-9,-5,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313338} {:answer/id #uuid "bc7ae479-5f79-5a12-800f-dfc0be27aceb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-19,-5,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313445} {:answer/id #uuid "ed86fa34-154a-507c-ade7-f09ae536f0b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,9,-5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313871}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bc7ae479-5f79-5a12-800f-dfc0be27aceb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-19,-5,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313445} :answer-field/id #uuid "919b5cd2-ecf2-59dc-9064-6e6d909d482b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314402}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "5873c215-84fe-562e-9b4f-b99d76cb6e63" :question/math-academy-id "q-33968" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨1,3,2⟩+w⟨-5,-2,-1⟩,\\,Π:r=⟨-12,10,6⟩+s⟨1,0,4⟩+t⟨2,6,0⟩.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "From the equation of a plane in the parametric form $r=p+tv+sw$, we have that its normal vector is $n=v\\times w.$ In our case, the normal vectors to $Π$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =⟨1,0,4⟩\\times ⟨2,6,0⟩ \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 6\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =-24i+8j+6k \\\\  & =⟨-24,8,6⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane $Π$ in dot product form is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-24,8,6⟩ & =⟨-12,10,6⟩\\cdot ⟨-24,8,6⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-24,8,6⟩ & =404.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨1,3,2⟩+w⟨-5,-2,-1⟩$ into the equation of the plane in dot product form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨-24,8,6⟩ & =404 \\\\ ⟨1-5w,3-2w,2-w⟩\\cdot ⟨-24,8,6⟩ & =404 \\\\ -24(1-5w)+8(3-2w)+6(2-w) & =404 \\\\ -24+120w+24-16w+12-6w & =404 \\\\ 98w & =392 \\\\ w & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $q$ of the intersection point $Q,$ we substitute $w=4$ into the vector equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}q & =⟨1-5(4),3-2(4),2-(4)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-19,-5,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is $Q(-19,-5,-2).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186475938 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119836 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "abef3da6-252e-51e4-b816-9ef7233b9a5d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line in Vector Form and a Plane in Dot Product Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4220dbdf-b64e-566f-ae49-56f619b94daf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,4,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475539} {:answer/id #uuid "a263b19c-dab2-51ad-a37c-4d7d02bba31d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,4,9)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475682} {:answer/id #uuid "b1727d54-c85a-57b8-a08b-528c454ea97c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1,4,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475704} {:answer/id #uuid "b314dcbd-c630-5e14-8975-1aa386fad831" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,4,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475708} {:answer/id #uuid "ea3afca3-5485-5e1f-b70b-ffd448191cf1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475802}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4220dbdf-b64e-566f-ae49-56f619b94daf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,4,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475539} :answer-field/id #uuid "49aa9793-d791-5a4c-9561-114186e2e854" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475854}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6079a48b-0752-583a-8f2a-84194653fec2" :question/math-academy-id "q-33972" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨2,4,-1⟩+t⟨1,4,3⟩,\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨3,12,9⟩=45.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's write the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨2+t,4+4t,-1+3t⟩.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨2+t,4+4t,-1+3t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨3,12,9⟩ & =45 \\\\ ⟨2+t,4+4t,-1+3t⟩\\cdot ⟨3,12,9⟩ & =45 \\\\ 3(2+t)+12(4+4t)+9(-1+3t) & =45 \\\\ 6+3t+48+48t-9+27t & =45 \\\\ 78t & =0 \\\\ t & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$ is obtained by substituting $t=0$ into the equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨2+(0),4+4(0),-1+3(0)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,4,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(2,4,-1).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186403738 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119836 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "abef3da6-252e-51e4-b816-9ef7233b9a5d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line in Vector Form and a Plane in Dot Product Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7d6e560d-c0f9-5b00-9374-501b77816db3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-5,-6,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403740} {:answer/id #uuid "0d5dad58-6f17-557a-a47c-3daedf8cd066" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,-6,7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403741} {:answer/id #uuid "697db66d-1d20-570e-bd42-19a3bff15801" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403742} {:answer/id #uuid "2a612b0e-faeb-5123-a818-5a85e0cc7103" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-5,2,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403743} {:answer/id #uuid "f4069451-0a02-5138-bd42-c9a8964d8236" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,2,7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403744}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "697db66d-1d20-570e-bd42-19a3bff15801" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403742} :answer-field/id #uuid "b8a46fca-92cb-569e-aaa5-ff42267626c0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403739}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "36894dd9-ad4f-58c5-8fd6-dfd9706bcecb" :question/math-academy-id "q-73984" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨3,2,7⟩+t⟨-5,-6,0⟩,\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨-6,5,4⟩=-24.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's write the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨3-5t,2-6t,7⟩.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨3-5t,2-6t,7⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨-6,5,4⟩ & =-24 \\\\ ⟨3-5t,2-6t,7⟩\\cdot ⟨-6,5,4⟩ & =-24 \\\\ -6(3-5t)+5(2-6t)+4\\cdot 7 & =-24 \\\\ -18+30t+10-30t+28 & =-24 \\\\ 20 & =-24.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation has no solution. Therefore, we conclude that the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ do not intersect."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186475955 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119838 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "82e761b5-ec1c-549d-b726-e0909cfe460b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line in Parametric Form and a Plane in Cartesian Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d3759ca-f415-569b-a33a-acb5640cdbd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(15,-17,13)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475527} {:answer/id #uuid "4d264b47-4019-5711-a224-f0cc582f5fc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,3,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475558} {:answer/id #uuid "95eb3494-b745-564b-b1bb-9df9395d27c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475667} {:answer/id #uuid "c1d7c847-242b-5cf2-ae20-6f260249b5dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(13,35,31)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475738} {:answer/id #uuid "da243a84-b978-5f29-8ece-2e8668c34cc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5,3,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475773}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3d3759ca-f415-569b-a33a-acb5640cdbd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(15,-17,13)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475527} :answer-field/id #uuid "380c38bf-f532-5171-bcc5-76a194ee6084" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475847}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b3b4f2c0-7489-5ff6-9c21-54c57d280888" :question/math-academy-id "q-73997" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:\\{\\begin{aligned}x=5-2t \\\\ y=8+5t \\\\ z=-7-4t\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:2x-3y+z-94=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-3y+z-94 & =0 \\\\ 2(5-2t)-3(8+5t)-7-4t & =94 \\\\ 10-4t-24-15t-7-4t & =94 \\\\ -23t & =115 \\\\ t & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=-5$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=5-2(-5)=15 \\\\ y=8+5(-5)=-17 \\\\ z=-7-4(-5)=13\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is  $P(15,-17,13).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186475941 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119838 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "82e761b5-ec1c-549d-b726-e0909cfe460b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line in Parametric Form and a Plane in Cartesian Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14828947-21b5-5b44-8ba4-a8c5ac78f5e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(7,3,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475474} {:answer/id #uuid "1d11cddd-41a7-59cd-a0f7-eb0c9bbb8aab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475480} {:answer/id #uuid "495e886a-52d9-5c59-8c47-3821329f3910" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(17,32,11)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475553} {:answer/id #uuid "ab4f8ebf-675e-5768-87c1-628fdd24f267" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,2,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475693} {:answer/id #uuid "dcf5feda-7db4-5eea-9893-715ff228f6be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(7,12,15)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475778}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "495e886a-52d9-5c59-8c47-3821329f3910" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(17,32,11)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475553} :answer-field/id #uuid "8d36f85e-f322-5625-a3c0-402881668478" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475874}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "789a0f9b-548a-5d80-a6d7-b592e86b7749" :question/math-academy-id "q-74001" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:\\{\\begin{aligned}x=2-3t \\\\ y=-3-7t \\\\ z=1-2t\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:-2x+4y-7z=17.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2x+4y-7z & =17 \\\\ -2(2-3t)+4(-3-7t)-7(1-2t) & =17 \\\\ -4+6t-12-28t-7+14t & =17 \\\\ -8t & =40 \\\\ t & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=-5$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=2-3(-5)=17 \\\\ y=-3-7(-5)=32 \\\\ z=1-2(-5)=11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is $P(17,32,11).$"}]}
